; Selling part of an unfixated lot at a fixated cost leaves the rest of
; the lot floating: the sale, `-10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] @ =$6`, names a
; lot its account holds, so it sells from that lot, and `@ =price`
; fixates only a lot it creates, never one the posting names.  The
; 10 AAPL left keep the lot {$5} [2020/01/01], and -V values them at the
; latest price, 10 x $7 = $70.
;
; 3.4.1 fixated the named lot itself, for every holder and from its
; purchase on, so the shares left showed as {=$5} [2020/01/01] and -V
; held them at their $5 lot price, $50, whatever the market did.

P 2020/03/01 AAPL $7

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    20 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/02/01 Sell
    Assets:Broker   -10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] @ =$6
    Assets:Cash      $60
    Income:Gains

test bal --lots Assets:Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]  Assets:Broker
end test

test bal -V Assets:Broker
                 $70  Assets:Broker
end test
